From above.

26
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:02,180
From next stage.

27
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:08,760
From east.

28
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,740
I remember the day when
everything changed.

29
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:29,674
The day I found out I wasn't
really part of this family.

30
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,820
It felt weird.

31
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,694
Like I didn't fit in with them anymore.

32
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,697
And I found this out.

33
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:39,420
when I was 10.

34
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,000
I'd wonder, who is she?

35
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,780
And do I really know anything about her?

36
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:57,740
Maybe that feeling I had of not fitting in

37
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:01,147
was the thing that drove
me to online gaming.

38
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:07,380
I guess I figured, in the virtual world,
no one knows anything about anyone.

39
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:11,340
So I dove right in, and thought
it was where I belonged.

40
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:17,046
But those two years I spent
trapped in SAO taught me something.

41
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:21,800
The difference between a real and
a virtual world is slim at best.

42
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:25,995
It's a waste of time asking
people who they really are.

43
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:30,480
All you can do is accept them
as is, and have faith in them.

44
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:35,420
Cause in the end, whoever you think
they are, that's who they really are.

45
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:40,417
When I got back to the real
world and saw Sugu's face.

46
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,360
I was really, truly happy.

47
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,817
Right then and there.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,257
I swore I'd do whatever I could!

49
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:51,337
To try to close the gap
that had grown between us.

50
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:53,440
Over the last couple of years?

51
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,920
